# The seven PDFs under arxiv_submission/ were committed as RAW BYTES, not as LFS
# pointers (main.pdf is 986123 bytes of %PDF-1.5 in the tree; a pointer is ~131).
# The `*.pdf filter=lfs` rule above therefore makes git clean the working copy
# into a pointer and compare that against the raw blob, so these files report as
# modified whenever anything touches their mtime — while being byte-identical to
# HEAD. Measured: after `touch arxiv_submission/*.pdf`, 7 modified without this
# rule, 0 with it, 7 again when removed.
#
# Unsetting the attributes here matches how the files are actually stored. The
# PDFs that ARE real pointers (_intake/, apps/web/src/routes/paper/) keep
# filter=lfs and are unaffected.
arxiv_submission/*.pdf !filter !diff !merge
